AlgebraicGeometry/AbelianVarieties/Homomorphisms/Integral.lean
--------------------------------------------------------------
New file (3ca2b4e). Line numbers as of 2026-10-22.
[ ] nameless                                                         (l.40)
      Stated as: IsIntegral ℤ φ₀ → φ₀ ∈ image of End (mk A).
      FALSE as stated: End A is an order, not the set of all integral
      elements. Counterexamples: [[0, 1/2], [0, 0]] in End⁰ (E × E)
      (nilpotent, so integral); (1 + √-3)/2 for E with CM by ℤ[√-3].
      The `have : n = 1` step fails too (fractions are not unique).
      The module docstring ("integral elements of End⁰ A are exactly
      End A") has to be corrected as well. True replacements:
        - every element of End A is integral over ℤ (IsIntegral.of_finite,
          needs fin_gen_hom);
        - (1/n) ⊗ₜ φ ∈ End A iff φ kills A[n] (needs isogenies).


